    {
      "id": "intro-1",
      "sectionId": "intro",
      "text": "Tap-tap, twig-twig—build a little nest beat.",
      "objective": "narration",
      "objectReveal": "none"
    },
    {
      "id": "intro-2",
      "sectionId": "intro",
      "text": "Bird names fly in where letters and wingbeats meet.",
      "objective": "narration",
      "objectReveal": "none"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-A",
      "sectionId": "r1-a-d",
      "text": "A is here; Albatross is why. Albatross in sight | feathers, beak, and feet give clues just right",
      "targetId": "A",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-B",
      "sectionId": "r1-a-d",
      "text": "Bluebird answers B. Bluebird is a feathered bird; beak and feet hint at how it lives.",
      "targetId": "B",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-C",
      "sectionId": "r1-a-d",
      "text": "across the open sky, what belongs to C? Crane! It is a feathered bird; beak and feet hint at how it lives.",
      "targetId": "C",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-D",
      "sectionId": "r1-a-d",
      "text": "D—short beat—Duck. Duck is a water-side bird; beak, legs, and feet fit its watery habitat.",
      "targetId": "D",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-E",
      "sectionId": "r1-e-h",
      "text": "Hear E; see Egret. Egret on the perch | bill and feet are clues we search",
      "targetId": "E",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-F",
      "sectionId": "r1-e-h",
      "text": "F is here; Flamingo is why. It is a long-legged water bird with a bent bill adapted for filter feeding.",
      "targetId": "F",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-G",
      "sectionId": "r1-e-h",
      "text": "Goldfinch answers G. Goldfinch is a feathered bird; beak and feet hint at how it lives.",
      "targetId": "G",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1-H",
      "sectionId": "r1-e-h",
      "text": "across the open sky, what belongs to H? Hummingbird! It is a tiny bird that can hover by beating its wings extremely fast.",
      "targetId": "H",
      "objective": "lexical-semantic",
      "objectReveal": "line-start"
    },
    {
      "id": "chorus-r1-2-1",
      "sectionId": "chorus-r1-2",
      "text": "Twig by twig, beat by beat!",
